{#def agent_id, accounts, redirect_url="", id_suffix="", can_add_account=False #}
{#
  Renders inside the sharing editor / workspace settings when the workspace
  has no associated account yet. Either prompts the user to pick an account
  to associate (if any are signed in) or links to sign-in/create-account.

  Behavior lives in /_static/associate.js, which binds every ``data-associate``
  prompt on the page independently. It is a static file, not an inline script,
  because the shell's page-swap engine only re-executes scripts from
  #local-page-scripts -- an inline one would be adopted and never run, leaving
  the form to do a native GET that looks like the button doing nothing. Any
  page that renders this component must load that script.

  ``id_suffix`` keeps element ids unique on a surface that renders MORE THAN
  ONE Associate -- the workspace options panel shows both the Share pane's
  prompt and the Machine settings account group at once. (The script scopes
  itself per prompt, so it does not depend on the suffix; the ids are still
  the contract other code and tests select on.)


  ``can_add_account`` adds an "Add account" entry to the account picker, for
  surfaces where signing in with another account is a reasonable next step
  rather than a detour. Off by default so existing callers are unchanged.
#}
{# Deliberately not a Card: this is a message and a button, and boxing it in a
   bordered surface framed it as a separate panel inside whichever pane it
   already sits in. #}
<div class="my-3">
  <p class="font-semibold mb-2">Link your machine to an Imbue account to enable sharing and cloud backups.</p>
  {% if accounts %}
    {# Associate the workspace with an account via a JSON PATCH to the v1
       workspace resource (account_id), then return to redirect_url (if set)
       or reload to show the associated state. #}
    <div data-associate data-agent-id="{{ agent_id }}" data-redirect-url="{{ redirect_url }}">
      <form id="associate-form{{ id_suffix }}" data-associate-form class="flex gap-2 items-center mt-2">
        <Select name="user_id" width="w-auto">
          {% for acct in accounts %}
            <option value="{{ acct.user_id }}">{{ acct.email }}</option>
          {% endfor %}
          {% if can_add_account %}
            <option value="{{ ADD_ACCOUNT_OPTION_VALUE }}">Add account...</option>
          {% endif %}
        </Select>
        <ButtonSubmit variant="primary">Link</ButtonSubmit>
      </form>
      <p id="associate-error{{ id_suffix }}" data-associate-error class="hidden type-body text-important mt-2" role="alert"></p>
    </div>
  {% else %}
    <div class="mt-3">
      <ButtonLink href="/auth/login" variant="primary">Sign in or create an account</ButtonLink>
    </div>
  {% endif %}
</div>
